{
  "about": "One constant offset on a right-hand fact, {offset: {fact: <path>, add|subtract: <magnitude>}} (docs/design/expression-family-source22.md, A2). `integer` and `timestamp` rows are `left <op> base +/- magnitude` over a row {left, base}; each lane builds the predicate {left: {<op>: {offset: {fact: base, <direction>: <magnitude>}}}} from them, and holds its faulty variants (wrap, clamp, binary64, Unknown on overflow, ignored sign, ignored unit, ignored base, field-minus-field) to disagree with at least one row. Answered by tests/offset_operand.rs, the Go fixture ess-conformance/tests/fixtures/offset-operand.go and ess-conformance/src/ts/predicate.test.ts.",
